{"id":"2026-11-02-aios-skill-fixes-2","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios-compare","context":"Claude and Codex compared the two audits. The rewrite is better, but the rerun made 3 errors: it called a byte count a char count (MEMORY.md 1,894 vs the real 1,865), it judged rules from Codex sessions it only counted, and it missed a 09-13 history note on the delete card. Fixes: (1) measure caps with Python len(); (2) list what each check read vs only counted; (3) one pointer result line per DELETE, history hits read too; (4) allow the STATUS.md line in the write list. Report: KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-11-02-compare.md","options":[{"detail":"Edit SKILL.md, Codex review, commit, push. No new audit run.","key":"a","label":"Apply the 4 fixes"},{"detail":"Next month's audit may repeat these 3 errors.","key":"b","label":"Leave the skill as is"}],"order":8,"question":"Apply 4 more small fixes to the aios-audit skill?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit","result":"Done: 4 fixes + doctor-plus note; Codex review 3 accepted, 1 reworded. KeystoneOS e48a07e.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.420889Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-ap-manual","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"Flint notes name it. It is not on disk or Drive.","options":[{"detail":"Put where it is in the note.","key":"a","label":"Yes, it exists"},{"detail":"I remove it from the playbook sources.","key":"b","label":"No, drop the reference"}],"order":7,"question":"Does the 'AP Assessment Manual V12' exist?","rec":"b","repo":"Performance_Playbook","result":"Dropped from docs/digest/sources.md. Flint notes still name it.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:28:31.917129Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-auburn-pdfs","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"They are tracked in the repo and may name athletes.","options":[{"detail":"Upload to FA2026/04_Outputs, add to .gitignore, git rm --cached.","key":"a","label":"Move to Drive and stop tracking"},{"detail":"No change.","key":"b","label":"Leave them in git"}],"order":4,"question":"Move the Auburn_G1_*.pdf reports out of git?","rec":"a","repo":"Catapult_API","result":"All 9 uploaded to Drive Football/FA2026/04_Outputs/Auburn_G1_2026-09-05 (checksums match), then untracked and gitignored. They stay on disk.","status":"closed"},"version":3,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:33:40.669398Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-dedupe-tier-a-indexes","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios-rerun","context":"13 project MEMORY.md files list most notes twice: once by title, once by filename. It is the same fix the first audit made in KeystoneOS today. No note is deleted; only the second index line goes. Worst: your home folder index (15), FaceComps (14 + 14 in the old Windows copy).","options":[{"detail":"Keep the title line, drop the filename line. Each note stays indexed once.","key":"a","label":"Yes, dedupe all 13"},{"detail":"No change. Each index stays longer than it needs to be.","key":"b","label":"Leave them"}],"order":2,"question":"Remove 74 double lines from 13 memory indexes?","rec":"a","repo":"~/.claude/projects/*/memory","result":"Done: 74 lines removed from 13 indexes; 0 doubles, 0 broken links left. dotclaude 0a68ee7a.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.388189Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-dev-repo-areas","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-drive-projects","context":"119 repos had commits in 90 days; 99 sit at ~/DEV top level. Moving them breaks absolute paths in scripts, launchd jobs and KeystoneOS discovery, and the plan puts it after the football season.","options":[{"detail":"Keep the plan. Same name rule then: folder = board name.","key":"a","label":"After the season (from 2027-01-15)"},{"detail":"Faster to navigate sooner. Each move needs a path sweep and checks; risk of breaking a live job mid-season.","key":"b","label":"Now, non-football repos only"}],"order":2,"question":"When should the 99 top-level ~/DEV repos move into Area folders?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 4","result":"Done 11-02 (dev-28): Program 21, Research 12, Performance 22 repos moved into Area folders. Kept at the top: SpecialRequests, LibraryProject (nested repos), DataBase_GPS_Reporting, ForcePlate_DecisionSystem, VALD_Performance (live pipelines). Platform is a new decision: 2026-11-02-platform-move.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T21:47:21.951413Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-doctor-plus-callable","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios-rerun","context":"rot.md gives the Context posture layer to doctor-plus. doctor-plus is set so only you can start it (disable-model-invocation), so the audit can never run it. That layer was last checked 2026-10-11. It already reports first and fixes only on approval.","options":[{"detail":"Remove disable-model-invocation; it stays name-only, so it adds no context. The audit calls it report-only.","key":"a","label":"Let the audit call it"},{"detail":"No change to the skill. rot.md says Eric runs it every 3 months.","key":"b","label":"I run /doctor-plus myself"}],"order":6,"question":"Let the AIOS audit run doctor-plus for you?","rec":"a","repo":"~/.claude/skills/doctor-plus","result":"Done: disable-model-invocation removed; still name-only. aios-audit runs it report-only. skills afbb99b.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.407822Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-generic-skills","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios","context":"Never used in Claude or Codex (checked again: 0 calls, 0 Codex reads). All 4 are hidden as name-only. The model already does each job. Pointers I would fix: ~/DEV/WORKFLOW.md line 108 (articulation-skill → ELI5 output style) and line 117 (/ISA, drop the row). ArXiv and Science: no live pointers. History: on 09-13 you turned ArXiv, ISA and Science back on only to fix Codex parity; that note says to retire a skill instead of hiding it. Reports: KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-11-02*.md","options":[{"detail":"I move them to ~/.claude/skills-archive (they can come back), fix the WORKFLOW.md row, commit, and push.","key":"a","label":"Delete all 4"},{"detail":"No change. They stay hidden and unused.","key":"b","label":"Keep them"}],"order":1,"question":"Delete 4 generic skills: ArXiv, Science, ISA, articulation-skill?","rec":"a","repo":"~/.claude/skills","result":"Kept (you chose b). No change.","status":"closed"},"version":5,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.370231Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-keystone-gps","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"The Windows laptop is retired from automation, so the Refresh_All_Data GPS step no longer runs. Three old GPS copies are listed in docs/audits/2026-09-13-gps-locations.md.","options":[{"detail":"I check each path first. Copies on the laptop stay listed.","key":"a","label":"Close it; move the Mac copies to _to_delete"},{"detail":"No change.","key":"b","label":"Leave it open"}],"order":9,"question":"Close the Windows GPS step and clear the 3 old GPS copies?","rec":"a","repo":"KeystoneOS","result":"Windows step closed. None of the 3 old copies are on the Mac (1 on Google Drive, 2 on Baylor OneDrive), so they stay your hand step.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:28:31.933915Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-maceverything-google-drive","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-maceverything","context":"Since 10-24, search skips Google Drive. Your main documents return 0 hits. That is likely why the app felt worse than Everything. It was turned off because the Drive folder made the search engine write about 27,000 errors to its log. The log is now trimmed each day, and no files were lost. The index stays on this Mac only.","options":[{"detail":"Add Google Drive in config.json. I check the error count after one day. If errors come back, I turn it off again.","key":"a","label":"Turn Drive back on (1-day trial)"},{"detail":"Search covers this Mac and drives only. Drive files stay unsearchable.","key":"b","label":"Keep Drive out"}],"order":23,"question":"MacEverything: search your Google Drive files again?","rec":"a","repo":"Personal/MacEverything","result":"Drive trial started 2026-11-03 00:21 UTC: config.json extraRoots = Google Drive account folder; daemon picked it up and is scanning. Check after 1 day: 'giving up' log lines since 00:21:47 (want 0). If they come back, remove config.json to turn Drive off.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-03T00:22:08.940318Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-name-only-rest","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios","context":"Name-only means Claude sees the name but not the description, so it only uses the skill when you or a routine call it by name. It keeps every session's context small. The metrics script now counts these separately (name_only=28, name_only_never_used=15), so they no longer look like bloat.","options":[{"detail":"No change. Small context stays small.","key":"a","label":"Keep name-only; call them by name"},{"detail":"Write the names in the note. Each one adds a little to every session's context.","key":"b","label":"Show descriptions for the ones I use"}],"order":2,"question":"The other 24 name-only skills: keep them name-only?","rec":"a","repo":"~/.claude/settings.json","result":"Kept name-only (a). No change.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.374625Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-pff-olddb","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"Since 10-08 the Mac reads ~/.local/share/pff-data/pff.db. Your condition was met on 10-31: weeks 4-8 pulled into the new DB with 0 failures. The old file only adds a 79-row ingest history.","options":[{"detail":"data/pff.db plus the three pff_before_* backups.","key":"a","label":"Delete the 4 files"},{"detail":"Nothing changes. 2.8 GB stays on disk.","key":"b","label":"Keep them for now"}],"order":2,"question":"Delete the old Mac PFF database and its 3 backups (about 2.8 GB)?","rec":"a","repo":"Football/PFF_Data_Project","result":"The 4 files were moved to ~/.Trash/PFF_old_db_2026-11-02 (the safety guard blocked a hard delete). Empty the Trash to free 2.8 GB.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:28:31.877623Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-pff-receiver","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"STATUS says the next real work is the 12-02 checkpoint.","options":[{"detail":"No work now.","key":"a","label":"At the 12-02 checkpoint"},{"detail":"One short session.","key":"b","label":"Look into it now"}],"order":12,"question":"The receiver id in the video feed does not match roster ids. When do we work it out?","rec":"a","repo":"Football/PFF_Position_Reports","result":"The id is team code + jersey (e.g. TXBA 01). It cannot match: the roster has no jersey numbers for any season. The next step is in STATUS.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:28:31.962565Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-platform-move","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-dev-areas","context":"Program, Research and Performance are moved. Platform is wired in by absolute path: 13 launchd jobs, KeystoneOS jobs.json, 2 hooks (the SessionStart memory injection reads ~/DEV/KeystoneOS), skills and scripts. One missed path breaks session startup or the nightly jobs.","options":[{"detail":"Move Platform with the Football repos and the 3 live pipelines in one orchestrated run: fix plists, jobs.json and hooks in the same pass, then re-test startup and every job.","key":"a","label":"After the season, one Workflow run"},{"detail":"Zero risk to automation. ~/DEV top keeps ~20 Platform folders, and the 'only Area folders at the top' goal is dropped for them.","key":"b","label":"Never: Platform stays at the DEV top"}],"order":1,"question":"When should the Platform repos (KeystoneOS, project-triage, claude-global-memory, drive-tools and the rest) move into ~/DEV/Platform/?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 4","result":"A (11-02): Platform, Football, the 3 live pipelines and 4 unrouted repos move after the season (from 2027-01-15) in one Workflow run that fixes plists, jobs.json, hooks and daily-backup in the same pass. Recorded in FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 4.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T21:53:37.107726Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-playbook-part3","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"The NCAA guide moved from Chris to Kenny on 10-07, so these are now Kenny's decisions. You sent a nudge on 10-31 and asked for a reply by Fri 11-07.","options":[{"detail":"I add it to the 11-05 list and fix the name in STATUS.","key":"a","label":"Ask Kenny at the 11-05 hour block"},{"detail":"No change.","key":"b","label":"Wait for the 11-07 reply"}],"order":6,"question":"Part 3 (NCAA) waits on 'Chris Ruf's three decisions'. Ask Kenny on 11-05 instead?","rec":"a","repo":"Performance_Playbook","result":"Added to the NCAA STATUS for the 11-05 hour block. Playbook STATUS now names Kenny.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:28:31.907496Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-project-folders","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-drive-projects","context":"Board has 13 active projects. Only 2 have a folder in 01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE; 3 sit in _STALLED; 8 have no Drive folder. 5 archived projects still sit in _ACTIVE. Work is spread over 6 top folders (Performance_Playbook in 3, RTP in up to 6). One project often has 3 names (board, DEV, Drive).","options":[{"detail":"One folder per active project, named YYYY-MM-DD_<board name>. Files elsewhere get a shortcut there (nothing breaks). Stalled/archived folders move out. A weekly drift check keeps it true. You run one --apply line in Terminal.","key":"a","label":"_ACTIVE mirrors the board"},{"detail":"A single page in _ACTIVE with links to each project's files. Cheaper, but it is a page, not folders.","key":"b","label":"One index page, no moves"}],"order":1,"question":"How should Drive show your live projects?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 12","result":"Done 2026-11-02: _ACTIVE now has one folder per active board row (13); archived folders moved to _STALLED; 6 shortcuts to ladder homes; drive_folder set on all 13 rows; drive_index.py active-check is clean and runs in weekly-review. Weekly_Matchups_2026 held in _ACTIVE until after the season (live football path).","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T22:04:34.462528Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-retire-project-triage","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios-rerun","context":"It builds the old DEV triage HTML page. It last wrote one on 2026-08-18. The live board (/project, board.py) does this job now. 0 Claude calls, 0 Codex reads. Three places point at it and I would fix them: project/SKILL.md line 8, ~/DEV/COMMANDS.md lines 405 and 434. Report: KeystoneOS/docs/audits/aios-audit-2026-11-02-rerun.md","options":[{"detail":"Move it to ~/.claude/skills-archive (it can come back), fix the 3 pointers, commit, push.","key":"a","label":"Retire it"},{"detail":"No change.","key":"b","label":"Keep it"}],"order":1,"question":"Retire the project-triage skill?","rec":"a","repo":"~/.claude/skills","result":"Done: moved to ~/.claude/skills-archive/project-triage; 3 pointers fixed (project/SKILL.md, COMMANDS.md x2). skills afbb99b, DEV cadd71a. The name-only line in settings.json stays (harmless).","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.384007Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-rule-paste-ready-commands","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios-rerun","context":"Twice this week a command failed when you pasted it. 11-02: a repo-relative path gave 'no such file or directory'. 10-31: a <words> placeholder gave 'parse error' in zsh. Rule text: 'A command handed to Eric runs when pasted from any folder: absolute paths, no <placeholders>.'","options":[{"detail":"One line under Workflow Expectations in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. Commit and push.","key":"a","label":"Add the rule"},{"detail":"No change.","key":"b","label":"No rule"}],"order":4,"question":"Add a rule: commands handed to you must work from any folder?","rec":"a","repo":"~/.claude/CLAUDE.md","result":"Done: rule added to ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. dotclaude 0a68ee7a.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.397834Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-rule-writing-for-agents","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios-rerun","context":"You asked for it 3 times in a week (10-26 twice, 10-29). Today only improve-system mentions it. Rule text: 'Auditing or improving a skill, CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md: use mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents.'","options":[{"detail":"One line in ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. Commit and push.","key":"a","label":"Add the rule"},{"detail":"Keep asking for it by name.","key":"b","label":"No rule"}],"order":5,"question":"Add a rule: skill audits use writing-for-agents?","rec":"a","repo":"~/.claude/CLAUDE.md","result":"Done: rule added to ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. dotclaude 0a68ee7a.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.403144Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-seed-notes","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios","context":"Notes/ has had no new note since 09-14. The audit's vault score fell to 63 (was 67 on 09-07) because of this. The oldest seed is planning-windows-compound.md (163 days).","options":[{"detail":"One card per note on this page. You click. Nothing moves without your click.","key":"a","label":"Yes: Claude proposes promote or archive for each"},{"detail":"No change. The vault score stays low.","key":"b","label":"Not now; after the season"}],"order":3,"question":"22 seed notes are older than 60 days. Sort them now?","rec":"a","repo":"SecondBrain/Notes","result":"Done: 22 cards seeded, batch 2026-11-02-seed-notes. All picks are promote.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.378873Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-small-router-fixes","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-aios-rerun","context":"(1) COMMANDS.md line 304 names a Playwright browser folder that is gone (chromium-1234; now 1243/1248). (2) WORKFLOW.md line 244 says DEV/CLAUDE.md still has a Desktop/DEV path; it does not. (3) Football/PFF_Position_Reports is an active repo no router names; add a FOOTBALL.md row. (4) Archive the j-2024 amniotic-membrane stub; the krystofiak-2024 brief is the full copy.","options":[{"detail":"Edit the 3 router lines, move the stub to Archive/, commit, push.","key":"a","label":"Do all 4"},{"detail":"No change.","key":"b","label":"Not now"}],"order":7,"question":"Make 4 small fixes to routers and the vault?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV + SecondBrain","result":"Done: COMMANDS.md browser line, WORKFLOW.md stale note, FOOTBALL.md row (DEV cadd71a); j-2024 stub archived (SecondBrain 450fee3).","status":"closed"},"version":3,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T20:06:09.413731Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-sr-pff","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"The email was built before these went on the ledger: the weekly PFF data pull is live (Wednesdays, weeks 4-8 pulled, 0 failures), and the position reports update is merged. The email is 222 words; the limit is 300.","options":[{"detail":"About 25 words. More Football credit. I rebuild the email, PDF and record.","key":"a","label":"Add one line"},{"detail":"No change. The PFF work goes in report #4 on 11-16.","key":"b","label":"Send as built"}],"order":1,"question":"Add one Football line for the two PFF items shipped late on 10-31?","rec":"a","repo":"Status report #3","result":"Send as built. The PFF items are noted in the record for report #4 (11-16).","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:28:31.869282Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-ssr-pdfs","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02","context":"List in docs/needs-eric.md section 1. One DOI (10.26603/ijspt20200326) is also unconfirmed because the check had a network error.","options":[{"detail":"I also re-check the DOI. You get only the paywalled rest.","key":"a","label":"Claude gets the open-access ones first"},{"detail":"No agent work.","key":"b","label":"I do all 24 myself"}],"order":8,"question":"24 PDFs in the library are the wrong articles. Who gets the right ones?","rec":"a","repo":"SportScienceResearchRepo","result":"14 of 24 replaced, and the DOI is confirmed. You still need 10 (7 paywalled, 3 browser-only); the list is in docs/pilot-screening/wrong-pdf-fetch-2026-11-02.md.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T18:28:31.924085Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-task11-annual-report-2025-2026","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-task11-names","context":"The name checker flags it because dated things should start with YYYY-MM-DD. But an annual report is named by its school year, not a day. The only date on hand is its last change on Drive (2026-10-09), which may not be the report's real date.","options":[{"detail":"New name 2026-10-09_Applied_Performance_AnnualReport_2025-2026.pdf. Uses the last-change date, which may not be the report's date.","key":"a","label":"Rename with the Drive date"},{"detail":"The school year is the right label for an annual report, and the name already searches well. It stays on the name-problem list; no date is guessed.","key":"b","label":"Keep the name"}],"order":25,"question":"Drive naming: rename Applied_Annual_Report_2025_2026.pdf (03_REPORTS/DEPARTMENT_ANNUAL_REPORT/Annual_Report_2026) to start with a date?","rec":"b","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 11","result":"B (11-02): name kept; the school year is its label. No rename.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T23:51:20.432779Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-task11-doc2-doc4","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-task11-names","context":"Two Word files from 2024-06-06 with no real name, so a search can never find them. The rename tool fixes only spaces and dates; it never guesses words. A real name needs someone to look inside each file.","options":[{"detail":"I open both files by the Drive API, propose one name each by the naming rules (e.g. 2024-06-06_Applied_Performance_AnnualReport_<part>.docx), and put the 2 names here for your yes.","key":"a","label":"I read them and propose names"},{"detail":"No change. They stay on the name-problem list. The annual-report folder name still tells you what they are.","key":"b","label":"Leave them as they are"}],"order":24,"question":"Drive naming: what should Doc2.docx and Doc4.docx in 03_REPORTS/DEPARTMENT_ANNUAL_REPORT/Annual_Report_2024 be called?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 11","result":"A (11-02): read both. Doc2 = first draft of the 2024 Executive Summary template; Doc4 = first draft of the Executive Summary. Both are older than ES_Template_Baylor_Applied_Performance.docx and ES_Baylor_Applied_Performance.docx in the same folder (not copies). Names proposed in 2026-11-02-task11-doc2-doc4-names.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T23:52:05.100645Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-task11-doc2-doc4-names","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-task11-names","context":"Both are first drafts from 2024-06-06 of the annual-report Executive Summary. The finished versions sit next to them (ES_Template_... and ES_Baylor_..., 06-06 and 06-07, longer). Both new names pass the name checker. On 10-30 you put old versions of NordBord and the YoY report in 10_ARCHIVE/2026/<name>_old_versions.","options":[{"detail":"I rename both now (rename tool, undo log). They stay in Annual_Report_2024 next to the finished versions.","key":"a","label":"Rename, keep in the folder"},{"detail":"I rename both, then you run one move command that puts them in 10_ARCHIVE/2026/Annual_Report_2024_old_versions. The 2024 folder keeps only the finished files.","key":"b","label":"Rename and archive as old drafts"}],"order":26,"question":"Rename Doc2.docx and Doc4.docx (Annual_Report_2024) to these names? Doc2 -> 2024-06-06_Applied_Performance_ExecutiveSummary_Template_Draft.docx; Doc4 -> 2024-06-06_Applied_Performance_ExecutiveSummary_Draft.docx","rec":"b","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 11","result":"B (Eric, in chat 11-02): Doc2/Doc4 renamed to 2024-06-06_Applied_Performance_ExecutiveSummary_Template_Draft.docx / _Draft.docx and moved to 10_ARCHIVE/2026/Annual_Report_2024_old_versions (filing_log: 2 moved; checked live).","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-02T23:54:55.460037Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-02-task12-mark-for-deletion","data":{"batch":"2026-11-02-task12-leftovers","context":"Your own folder of things to delete. 97 are shortcuts (deleting one never touches the real file). 182 are exact copies of kept files. 112 are one-of-a-kind (2 GB). 6 are shared with other people: deleting a shared file you own removes it for them too, so those 6 are always yours to check by hand. No name matches the health words.","options":[{"detail":"Trash the 97 shortcuts and 182 copies. Park the 112 one-of-a-kind files in 10_ARCHIVE/_PARKED_COPIES (same rule as earlier parks: delete after 2027-01-15 if never opened). Leave the 6 shared items for you. Needs a small tool change, Codex-reviewed, then one command from you.","key":"a","label":"Safe pass: copies out, rest parked"},{"detail":"Your label already says delete. Trash 385 items now (Drive keeps them 30 days, then they are gone). The 6 shared items stay for you.","key":"b","label":"Trash all but the 6 shared"}],"order":28,"question":"Drive root 'Mark for deletion' (391 items, 5 GB, 2014-2026): how far do we go?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md Task 12","result":"Done 11-03: 183 copies + 97 shortcuts trashed; of the 9 shared items, the 2 research PDFs already in Zotero (byte-identical) trashed (Eric 11-03); the folder (110 files) parked as 10_ARCHIVE/_PARKED_COPIES/2026-11-03_Mark_for_deletion. Sharing unchanged. Delete after 2027-01-15 if never opened.","status":"closed"},"version":3,"updatedAt":"2026-11-03T18:29:28.424379Z"}
