{"id":"2026-11-03-computers-dev-backups","data":{"batch":"2026-11-03-computers","context":"They are Drive-for-desktop backups of ~/DEV from this Mac (46,509 files) and the old Windows laptop (108,901), made before backups went off on 10-23. Drive search shows them next to your real files. Checked by fingerprint: 52,815 are the same as files on this Mac now; 66,000 are printing-press-library (on GitHub); 25,600 are rebuildable code parts; 4,000 are older versions of files you still have. About 5,700 are gone from the Mac: mostly agent session data, logs and build output, plus a morning-briefing/secrets folder (1,043 files; secrets should not be on Drive). 622 files sit in health-data paths and are never touched by a tool. Drive will not move backup files into My Drive, only copy them.","options":[{"detail":"First copy the few real documents found only there (PDF, Excel, Word, CSV, PowerPoint) into 10_ARCHIVE/2026/From_Computers. Then trash the rest, after a live check (Drive Trash keeps it 30 days). The 622 health-path files stay for you to look at. If any key in the secrets folder is still in use, rotate it.","key":"a","label":"Trash both DEV backups"},{"detail":"Nothing changes. They stay out of your main folders but keep showing in Drive search, and the secrets folder stays on Drive.","key":"b","label":"Leave them"}],"order":34,"question":"Drive 'Computers' holds 2 old DEV backups (155,000 files, 25 GB). Trash them?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md (Task 14)","result":"A applied 11-03: 26 documents found only in the backups copied to 10_ARCHIVE/2026/From_Computers; then 319 items (whole repos and folders) trashed from My Mac/DEV and My Laptop (2)/DEV, all confirmed. 5 health-named items kept untouched. The secrets folder is in Drive Trash (30 days): rotate any key in it that is still in use. Left: trash the non-DEV originals now copied to the archive, after the next index rebuild.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-03T22:03