{"id":"2026-11-03-computers-dev-backups","data":{"batch":"2026-11-03-computers","context":"They are Drive-for-desktop backups of ~/DEV from this Mac (46,509 files) and the old Windows laptop (108,901), made before backups went off on 10-23. Drive search shows them next to your real files. Checked by fingerprint: 52,815 are the same as files on this Mac now; 66,000 are printing-press-library (on GitHub); 25,600 are rebuildable code parts; 4,000 are older versions of files you still have. About 5,700 are gone from the Mac: mostly agent session data, logs and build output, plus a morning-briefing/secrets folder (1,043 files; secrets should not be on Drive). 622 files sit in health-data paths and are never touched by a tool. Drive will not move backup files into My Drive, only copy them.","options":[{"detail":"First copy the few real documents found only there (PDF, Excel, Word, CSV, PowerPoint) into 10_ARCHIVE/2026/From_Computers. Then trash the rest, after a live check (Drive Trash keeps it 30 days). The 622 health-path files stay for you to look at. If any key in the secrets folder is still in use, rotate it.","key":"a","label":"Trash both DEV backups"},{"detail":"Nothing changes. They stay out of your main folders but keep showing in Drive search, and the secrets folder stays on Drive.","key":"b","label":"Leave them"}],"order":34,"question":"Drive 'Computers' holds 2 old DEV backups (155,000 files, 25 GB). Trash them?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md (Task 14)","result":"A applied 11-03: 26 documents found only in the backups copied to 10_ARCHIVE/2026/From_Computers; then 319 items (whole repos and folders) trashed from My Mac/DEV and My Laptop (2)/DEV, all confirmed. 5 health-named items kept untouched. The secrets folder is in Drive Trash (30 days): rotate any key in it that is still in use. Left: trash the non-DEV originals now copied to the archive, after the next index rebuild.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-03T22:03:54.679679Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-03-drive-edit-watch","data":{"batch":"2026-11-03-arc-prep","context":"You edit on Drive from the Mac and Windows. Right now the print packet PDF only updates when you ask. The Drive API shows when each file was last edited, so a Mac job can check it. The PDF step needs Word on the Mac, and the Mac must be awake.","options":[{"detail":"A Mac job checks the 5 files every 30 minutes until Thu 11/05 noon. When one changes, it pulls the new versions, rebuilds the packet PDF on the Mac and on Drive, and texts you. Then it turns itself off. Small build, Codex-reviewed.","key":"a","label":"This packet only, until Thursday"},{"detail":"A watch list of Drive files for any project. The same check runs all the time. A changed file is pulled into its repo, and you get a text. You can reuse it, but it is a bigger build and one more scheduled job to keep healthy.","key":"b","label":"A standing Drive watcher"}],"order":32,"question":"When you edit a packet file on Drive, should the Mac notice and rebuild by itself?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/Program/BAIR_Steering_Committee","result":"A (11-03): live. launchd com.erash11.arcpacketwatch runs scripts/watch_packet_1105.py every 30 min and at Thu 11/05 12:00 Central, then removes itself. On a Drive edit it rebuilds the packet (new _r<MMDD-HHMM> file in 04_Committee), replaces the Drive packet content (same link) and texts you. Codex 5 rounds. Commit 5a785ad.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-03T20:23:01.035329Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-03-drive-fold-small","data":{"batch":"2026-11-03-drive-next","context":"Empty folders in 10_ARCHIVE and 99_UNSORTED (496 trees) are being trashed now: nothing is lost. Folding 1-2 file folders is different. Most of them (about 27,000) are inside code project copies or _MACHINE backups, where folding breaks the code or the backup. About 1,600 are in 10_ARCHIVE. There the folder name often says what the file is (for example '2019 Conference / slides.pdf'), and folding loses that. Drive search finds files by name either way, so folding does not help search.","options":[{"detail":"Keep the 1-2 file folders as they are. Task 13 ends after the empty folders. Nothing to undo, no names lost.","key":"a","label":"Skip folding"},{"detail":"Move each file up one level, renamed 'Folder - file', then trash the empty folder. About 1,600 folders. New code, a Codex review, about 30 min of run time.","key":"b","label":"Fold in 10_ARCHIVE only"}],"order":33,"question":"Drive: fold the folders that hold only 1-2 files into their parent folder?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md (Task 13 phase 2)","result":"A applied 11-03: no folding. 1-2 file folders stay as they are. Task 13 closed.","status":"closed"},"version":2,"updatedAt":"2026-11-03T18:14:25.266989Z"}
{"id":"2026-11-03-drive-next-step","data":{"batch":"2026-11-03-drive-next","context":"Measured 11-03: the top is already small (11 folders, 4 to 18 subfolders each). The noise is elsewhere: 65,000 of 83,500 items in 01_PROJECTS are code machinery inside 13 old project copies (37,950 node_modules + 18,330 .venv files, rebuildable; 8,625 .git files, kept). Plus 5,991 folders with only 1-2 items and 268 empty ones. Drive search looks at names, not folders, so bigger buckets help clicking, not searching.","options":[{"detail":"Trash the ~56,400 rebuildable code files (node_modules, .venv) in the 13 stalled/done project copies, after checking each repo is on GitHub. Then fold the 1-2 item folders and empty folders in 10_ARCHIVE and 01_PROJECTS into their parent. Top folders stay as they are. Index rebuild first; Codex-reviewed plan; you run --apply.","key":"a","label":"Clear the noise first"},{"detail":"Combine top folders (11 to about 6, e.g. 06_TEMPLATES into 05_SYSTEMS, 08_ADMIN into 03_REPORTS). Fewer clicks at the top, but a large move: script paths and links change, and the code noise stays. Best after the season.","key":"b","label":"Merge into bigger buckets"}],"order":32,"question":"Drive, next step: make the buckets bigger, or clear the noise first?","rec":"a","repo":"~/DEV/docs/FILE-ORGANIZATION-PLAN.md (new Task 13)","result":"Done 11-03. Phase 1: 18 rebuildable code folders (~56,000 items) trashed. Phase 2: 510 empty folder trees in 10_ARCHIVE and 99_UNSORTED trashed (2 shared skipped; second pass found 0 new). Folding skipped (Eric, A on 2026-11-03-drive-fold-small). Task 13 closed.","status":"closed"},"version":4,"updatedAt":"2026-11-03T18:14:25.278889Z"}
